 Madhurima's analysis (First Bug):

doc id - b896cb9f-b70e-48c5-b9b1-477aa18bf03a
 
I am checking some IBAT tool call cases, noticed that some issues. For example this one   "metadata": {       "primary_esn": "804699",       "primary_equip_type": "Gas Turbine",       "esn_confidence…
`1 Turbine` is matched by the generic subsection regex in [preprocessor_v2.py], and that path currently hard-codes the equipment type to `Gas Turbine` for every bare `Turbine` subsection. So when the document has:
 
- `STEAM TURBINE (814638 | SY0052637)`
- `1 Turbine`
the parser still labels that span as Gas Turbine, which then conflicts with the section path that correctly says it sits under the steam-turbine header.
 
I checked the b896cb9f-b70e-48c5-b9b1-477aa18bf03a case. The root cause is that the preprocessor is treating bare 1 Turbine subsections as Gas Turbine by default, even when they sit under a STEAM TURBINE header. That makes the section path and the equipment type disagree.
The fix is to make bare Turbine subsections inherit the nearest explicit equipment header above them instead of forcing them to Gas Turbine. That keeps gas-turbine docs unchanged, and it should correctly label the steam-turbine 1 Turbine section as Steam Turbine.
